t — one more possibility I haven't probed: \"The Letters of William and Dorothy Wordsworth, ed. Knight (1907)\" — PG? no. \"The Journals of Dorothy Wordsworth, ed. Knight (1897)\" — PG? no. \"The Poetical Works of William Wordsworth, ed. Knight (1882-89)\" — PG? no. \"The Life of William Wordsworth, Knight (1889)\" — PG? no. \"Wordsworthiana\" (1889) — PG? no. \"The English Lake District as Interpreted in the Poems of Wordsworth\" Knight (1878) — PG? no.\n\n\"Prose Works of Wordsworth\" (Grosart 1876) — PG? hmm... I said no. Let me just double-check my gut: I genuinely don't recall PG hosting it. OK.\n\n\"Memoirs of William Wordsworth\" (1851) — PG? no.\n\n\"Christopher Wordsworth, Memoirs\" covered.\n\n\"William Wordsworth: A Biography\" Knight covered.\n\n\"Wordsworth\" Myers EML (1881) — PG? probe... I don't recall it. no.\n\n\"Southey\" Dowden EML (1879) — PG? no.\n\n\"Coleridge\" Traill EML (1884) — PG? no.\n\n\"De Quincey\" Masson EML (1881) — PG? no.\n\n\"Hazlitt\" Birrell EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Lamb\" Ainger EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Scott\" Hutton EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Keats\" Colvin EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Shelley\" Symonds EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Byron\" Nichol EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Gray\" Gosse EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Goldsmith\" Black EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Johnson\" Stephen EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Gibbon\" Morison EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Hume\" Huxley EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Defoe\" Minto EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Richardson\" Dobson EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Fielding\" Dobson EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Sterne\" Traill EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Smollett\" Hannay EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Locke\" Fowler EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Berkeley\" Fraser EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Adam Smith\" Hirst EML — PG? no.\n\n\"Burke\" Morley EML — PG? #? hmm, \"Burke\" by John Morley EML — no relevance. skip.\n\nOK, truly done.\n\nHmm — so I deliver 5. Let me also double check the 5 URLs' format: \"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/57664/pg57664.txt\" (user's example format) ✔; others: \"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/583/pg583.txt\", \".../12145/pg12145.txt\",