rland and Cumberland\" (1777)\n12. Thomas Denton - \"A Perambulation of Cumberland\" (1687-8)\n13. Edmund Sandford - \"A Cursory Relation of all the Antiquities and Familyes in Cumberland\" (c. 1675)\n14. Camden's Britannia (1607/1610) - chorography mentioning Cumberland\n15. John Speed - \"The Theatre of the Empire of Great Britain\" (1611)\n16. Michael Drayton - \"Poly-Olbion\" (1612/1622) - includes Cumberland/Westmorland\n17. Daniel Defoe - \"A Tour thro' the Whole Island of Great Britain\" (1724-27) - Gutenberg #? Defoe's tour is on Gutenberg. Volume 3 covers the north. PG IDs: I believe \"Tour through the Eastern Counties\" is #? Not sure. Actually there's \"From London to Land's End\" etc. The whole \"A Tour Through the Whole Island of Great Britain\" is on Gutenberg as #? I don't remember the exact ID.\n18. Arthur Young - \"A Six Months' Tour through the North of England\" (1770) - includes Lake District descriptions\n19. Nathaniel Spencer (Robert Sanders) - \"The Complete English Traveller\" (1771)\n20. William Hutchinson - \"An Excursion to the Lakes\" (1774/1776)\n21. William Combe - \"The Tour of Dr. Syntax in Search of the Picturesque\" (1809)\n22. John Claudius Loudon - encyclopedias mention Lakes\n23. Ann Radcliffe - \"A Journey Made in the Summer of 1794\" (1795) - includes Lake District\n24. Sarah Murray - \"A Companion and Useful Guide to the Beauties of Scotland\" - not Lakes. But she did \"A Companion, and Useful Guide to the Beauties in the West Highlands of Scotland...\" Hmm.\n25. Elizabeth Smith? \n26. Mary Robinson? \n27. James Plumptre - \"The Lakers\" (1798) - a comic opera/play about Lake tourism! Real.\n28. William Green - \"Seventy-eight Studies from Nature\" (1809); \"A Description of a Series of Prints... The English Lakes\" (1814)\n29. William Ford - \"Description of Scenery in the Lake District\" (1839)\n30. Jonathan Otley - \"A Descriptive Guide to the English Lakes\" (1823)\n31. Harriet Martineau - \"A Complete Guide to the English